1.2 Execution Timestamp

For the purposes of this Agreement, "Execution Timestamp" shall refer to the precise date and time when an over-the-counter derivative contract is executed, as recorded in accordance with the following standards:

1.2.1 The Execution Timestamp shall be recorded in the format of "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS" in the Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) zone.

1.2.2 The Execution Timestamp shall be recorded by the Executing Party responsible for the execution of the contract, and shall be promptly provided to the other party upon request.

1.2.3 The following information shall be included as part of the Execution Timestamp:

(a) The name of the Executing Party, as identified in the Agreement, or the name of the authorized representative executing the contract on behalf of the Executing Party (in this case, "Gianpietro Fagiani-Versace");

(b) The unique identifier of the contract, as assigned in accordance with the standards set forth in the Agreement;

(c) The street address of the Executing Party, as identified in the Agreement (in this case, "71397 Solis Mission Apt. 625");

(d) The International Bank Account Number (IBAN) of the Executing Party, as identified in the Agreement (in this case, "GB61ZCFT08504835203703");

1.2.4 The Execution Timestamp shall be deemed to be accurate and binding on the parties, and shall be used for the purposes of record-keeping and regulatory compliance. Any discrepancies or disputes regarding the Execution Timestamp shall be resolved in accordance with the dispute resolution provisions set forth in the Agreement.
